BANKWISE DEMO BANK
DEBIT CARD SERVICES GUIDE

1. INTRODUCTION

A debit card is a banking card that allows eligible customers to access funds available in their linked bank account. Debit cards can generally be used for ATM withdrawals, purchases, and supported online transactions.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. DEBIT CARD FEATURES

Common debit card services may include:

• ATM cash withdrawals
• Balance enquiry
• Point-of-sale purchases
• Online purchases
• Contactless payments where supported
• Card management through mobile or internet banking
• International transactions where enabled

Available features depend on the card type and bank.

3. DEBIT CARD ACTIVATION

Customers should follow their bank's official procedure to activate a new debit card.

Activation may be available through:
• Bank ATM
• Mobile banking application
• Internet banking
• Official customer support
• Bank branch

Customers should never share their PIN or other confidential authentication information with anyone.

4. USING A DEBIT CARD

For a purchase, customers should verify the transaction amount before confirming it.

For online purchases, customers should use only trusted websites and check that the website is legitimate before entering payment information.

5. CONTACTLESS PAYMENTS

Some debit cards support contactless payments. Customers can use the card at compatible payment terminals by following the instructions provided by the bank and payment network.

Transaction limits and authentication requirements may apply.

6. ATM WITHDRAWALS

Debit cards can generally be used at supported ATMs to withdraw cash.

ATM withdrawal limits may depend on:
• Card type
• Account type
• Bank policy
• Customer settings
• ATM network

Customers should check the current limits through official banking channels.

7. FAILED CARD TRANSACTION

A debit card transaction may fail because of insufficient balance, incorrect information, technical problems, network issues, merchant restrictions, or other reasons.

If a transaction fails but money is deducted from the account, the customer should:
• Record the transaction details.
• Check the transaction status through official banking channels.
• Contact the bank if the issue is not resolved.

8. LOST OR STOLEN DEBIT CARD

If a debit card is lost or stolen, the customer should report it immediately.

The card may be blocked through an official:
• Mobile banking application
• Internet banking service
• Bank helpline
• Bank branch

Customers should follow the bank's official replacement procedure.

9. DAMAGED DEBIT CARD

If a debit card is damaged or no longer works properly, the customer can contact the bank to request a replacement.

The bank may have specific replacement procedures and applicable charges.

10. EXPIRED DEBIT CARD

Debit cards have an expiry date printed on the card. Customers should follow the bank's official procedure for replacement when the card approaches expiry.

Replacement procedures may vary depending on the bank and card type.

11. CARD SECURITY

Customers should protect their debit card and confidential information.

Never share:
• Card PIN
• OTP
• CVV
• Internet banking password
• UPI PIN
• Card authentication codes

Bank staff should not require customers to disclose confidential authentication credentials.

12. ONLINE DEBIT CARD SAFETY

Before making an online payment:
• Verify the website or application.
• Check the payment amount.
• Avoid suspicious links.
• Do not save card information on untrusted websites.
• Never share OTPs with another person.

13. UNAUTHORIZED TRANSACTION

If a customer notices a transaction that they do not recognize, they should contact the bank immediately through an official channel.

The customer should provide relevant transaction information requested by the bank but should never disclose passwords, PINs, or OTPs to unauthorized persons.

14. INTERNATIONAL TRANSACTIONS

Some debit cards may support international transactions.

International usage may need to be enabled through the bank's official application or another supported channel.

Foreign transactions may involve additional fees or exchange-rate considerations.

15. DEBIT CARD LIMITS

Banks may provide different limits for:
• ATM withdrawals
• Point-of-sale purchases
• Online transactions
• Contactless transactions
• International transactions

Customers should check their current card limits using official banking channels.

16. BANKWISE AI LIMITATION

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot created for a demonstration RAG project.

It cannot:
• Access real debit cards
• View customer accounts
• Block a real card
• Activate a real card
• Perform transactions
• Retrieve card details
• Process payments

For real card-related issues, customers should contact their actual bank through an official channel.

